Z||000000||sk8rpunk48162||11-02-2000||06:43 PM||||i have a 1986 fiero se and i wondered what kind of fuse to use for the radio.... please reply... send me icq or email please||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||11-02-2000||08:51 PM||||Simple solution. Get to know your fuse box.  A really cool design feature is if you squeeze the two tabs on either side of the fuse box, it swings down so you don't have to herniate a disk crawling under you dash to read it.  There is also a dandy storage area in the fuse box to store spare fuses.  I believe the fuse is a 10 amp.  Also realize that the same fuse for the radio controls the speedometer. <BR>Now if you are talking about what size inline fuse to use with an aftermarket stereo, use whatever the manufacturer tells you to.<P>Anyway, welcome to the forum, feel free to ask all kinds of questions and be prepared to get plenty of help. <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
